    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "CBPM Real Estate is delighted to bring to the market this spacious 4-bedroom, 3-bathroom semi-detached family home, ideally positioned within the popular Derrywood development in the picturesque village of Durrow, Co. Laois.\n\nBuilt in 2002, extending to 127.42 m² (1,371.5 sq. ft.) and with a BER rating of C, this attractive property offers generous and versatile accommodation throughout, combining comfortable family living with excellent practical features including a large kitchen/dining room, spacious living room, four well-proportioned bedrooms, three bathrooms, adjoining garage and a generous enclosed rear garden. The property benefits from oil-fired central heating.\n\nOn entering the property, a welcoming entrance hall leads through to the main living accommodation. The spacious front living room enjoys excellent natural light from the large window overlooking the front of the property, while a feature fireplace creates an attractive focal point and gives the room a warm and inviting feel.\n\nTo the rear lies the impressive kitchen and dining area, a particularly generous space ideally suited to everyday family life and entertaining. The fitted kitchen provides an excellent range of storage and worktop space, complemented by a substantial breakfast bar offering additional preparation space and casual seating. There is ample room for a full dining suite, while large sliding patio doors allow natural light to fill the room and provide direct access to the rear garden, creating an easy connection between the indoor and outdoor living spaces.\n\nThe accommodation continues across the upper floors with four bedrooms, offering plenty of flexibility for family living, guest accommodation or working from home. Built-in storage is provided within the bedroom accommodation, while the elevated position of the property allows for pleasant views from a number of the rooms.\n\n\nThe property benefits from three bathrooms, including the main family bathroom with bath and overhead shower, together with additional shower facilities. The upper accommodation, with its Velux windows and sloping ceilings, adds further character to the home while providing valuable additional living space.\n\nA particularly useful feature is the adjoining garage, which has electricity, lighting and internal access from the house. Whether retained for secure parking and storage or utilised as a practical hobby or workspace, it provides an excellent addition to the property.\n\nOutside, the property offers off-street parking to the front, together with a lawned area. To the rear is a generous, enclosed garden, providing excellent space for children, pets, outdoor dining and entertaining, with plenty of scope for a future patio, play area or further landscaping. Side access provides additional convenience.\n\nDerrywood is an established residential development conveniently positioned within the picturesque village of Durrow. The village offers a good range of everyday amenities and services, including shops, pharmacy, primary school, cafés, sporting and community facilities, while the surrounding area offers attractive countryside and walking amenities.\n\nDurrow is particularly well positioned for access to surrounding towns and the wider road network. Abbeyleix is approximately 510 minutes away, while Portlaoise is approximately 2025 minutes, providing an extensive selection of shopping, schools, restaurants, leisure facilities and rail services. Kilkenny City is approximately 3035 minutes away, offering further employment, retail and recreational amenities.\nFor commuters, the property enjoys convenient access to both major motorway networks, with the M8 approximately 15 minutes away and the M7 at Portlaoise approximately 2025 minutes away. The N77 provides the principal connection through Durrow towards Abbeyleix and Portlaoise, making the property a particularly convenient base for those travelling throughout Laois, Kilkenny and further afield.\n\nCombining the convenience of an established residential setting with excellent accessibility, 23 Derrywood offers an attractive balance between village living and easy access to larger towns, employment centres and transport links.\nWith its four-bedroom accommodation, three bathrooms, generous kitchen/dining area, adjoining garage, off-street parking and substantial rear garden, 23 Derrywood represents an excellent opportunity for families seeking a spacious and practical home in a well-established Durrow location.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\n\nDownstairs\n\nHallway 4.14m x1.52m Tiled floor, chandelier\nLiving Room 5.03m x 4.60m Carpet, ceiling rose, light fitting, fireplace, solid wood carved mantle, curtain & curtain pole, blind\nOpen plan kitchen & dining 3.71m x 6.21m - tiled floor, recessed lighting, light fitting, sliding door off dining room leading to back garden, curtain & curtain pole, fully fitted kitchen, fitted electric hob & oven, hob extractor, blind\nLaundry Room 2.00m x 1.93m Tiled floor, light fitting, guest w.c., door leading to attached garage\nGuest W.C. 2.05m x 0.90m Tiled floor, light fitting, w.h.b., w.c., tiled splashback\n\nUpstairs\n\nLanding 3.07m x 3.46m Carpet, light fitting\nMain Bedroom 3.97m x 2.97m Lino flooring, light fitting, Velux window\nEnsuite 1.52m x 2.96m Wood floor, light fitting, Velux window, shower cubicle, electric shower, w.c., w.h.b., tiled splashback, fitted mirror\nMain Bathroom 1.97m x 3.43m Tiled flooring, light fitting, half-wall tiled, w.h.b., fitted mirror, w.c., fitted bath, overhead shower, blind, glass shelves\nBedroom 2 3.55m x 2.68m Lino floor, light fitting, blind\nBedroom 3 3.42m x 3.38m Wood floor, light fitting, fitted wardrobes, curtain & curtain rail, blind\nBedroom 4 4.35m x 2.71m Carpet, light fitting\n\nAttached Garage 5.23m x 2.98m Lighting, electricity, shelving\n"
      },
